    content: # code-reviewer — Root orchestrator recipe
# Multi-agent code review system with parallel reviewers + aggregator

name: code-reviewer
title: Code-Reviewer Orchestrator
description: >
  Multi-agent code review system. Dispatches code to 4 parallel
  reviewer agents (style, security, perf, test) and aggregates
  results into a prioritized report with score and decision.

settings:
  timeout: 120
  max_steps: 30
  temperature: 0.3

extensions:
  - type: builtin
    name: developer
    bundled: true
  - name: summon
    type: platform

instructions: |
  You are the CODE-REVIEWER orchestrator. You coordinate a team of
  5 sub-agents to perform comprehensive code review.

  # EXECUTION MODEL — REQUIRED PARALLEL ARCHITECTURE
  #
  # The 4 reviewer agents have NO dependencies and MUST run in PARALLEL.
  # Use subagent delegation with async=true for all 4 simultaneously.
  # The review-aggregator runs AFTER all 4 reviewers complete.

  ## Step 1: Parallel review
  Delegate to 4 agents in PARALLEL:
   1. style-reviewer   → lint, formatting, naming, imports, dead code
   2. security-reviewer → vulns, secrets, XSS, SQLi (MANDATORY GATE)
   3. perf-reviewer     → performance, O(n^2), caching, I/O
   4. test-reviewer     → test coverage, edge cases, mocking

  ## Step 2: Collect results (wait for all 4)

  ## Step 3: Aggregate via review-aggregator
  - Merges issues sorted by severity
  - Calculates score (0-100)
  - Makes decision: approve | request_changes | needs_discussion

  ## Step 4: Return final result

  IMPORTANT: 4 reviewers MUST be parallel. Aggregator runs AFTER all complete.
  Security is a mandatory gate. Never say "I cannot review."

recipe_type: orchestrator
version: 1.0.0
sub_agents:
  - style-reviewer
  - security-reviewer
  - perf-reviewer
  - test-reviewer
  - review-aggregator
parallel_groups:
  - name: reviewers
    agents:
      - style-reviewer
      - security-reviewer
      - perf-reviewer
      - test-reviewer
  - name: aggregation
    depends_on: reviewers
    agents:
      - review-aggregator

returns:
  type: object
  properties:
    score:
      type: integer
      minimum: 0
      maximum: 100
    decision:
      type: string
      enum: ["approve", "request_changes", "needs_discussion"]
    summary:
      type: string
    all_issues_sorted:
      type: array


